ctus and KIID/KID must state its transparency policy, including whether it publishes full holdings daily or uses a periodic route, and how this relates to tracking and the ETF's market-making model.\n\n- **Daily public holdings:** Standard UCITS ETFs typically publish full portfolio holdings daily on the website, with NAV and indicative values intraday.\n\n- **Conditional periodic-holdings route:** Where permitted, a fund may publish holdings less often (for example, monthly or quarterly) but must provide daily basket or portfolio composition files to authorised participants and market makers so arbitrage works. The exact conditions and frequencies are set by the CBI rules and should be checked against the 2026 text.","ttft_ms":2747,"type":"result","duration_ms":4346,"uuid":"40fa9610-635c-419b-a78d-8a82cf82295a","ttft_stream_ms":425,"time_to_request_ms":53,"first_content_frame_ms":425,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
